326e5508-46d8-4c68-8e45-d0a193666d61	e7b51fed-62ad-4cc2-9361-40615c960616	`useState` Hook: Troubleshooting React State Update Issues	I'm experiencing issues with React's `useState` hook where the state doesn't seem to update properly, especially when dealing with rapid consecutive updates or asynchronous operations.\n\n## The Problem:\nWhen I click a button multiple times quickly to increment a counter, the state updates seem to be "skipped" or delayed. The counter doesn't reflect the actual number of clicks.\n\n## Code Example:\n```javascript\nfunction Counter() {\n  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);\n  \n  const handleClick = () => {\n    setCount(count + 1);\n    console.log('Current count:', count); // Always logs the previous value\n  };\n  \n  return (\n    <div>\n      <p>Count: {count}</p>\n      <button onClick={handleClick}>Increment</button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n\n**Expected Behavior**:\nEach button click should increment the counter by 1\n\nThe displayed count should match the number of clicks\n\nConsole should log the updated count value	\N	open	11	2025-10-26 07:47:06.747489-07	2025-10-26 09:34:38.450533-07	\N	\N	1	1
